Thought someone might be interested in this. Here are some useful
Xterm bindings for use with hack. add them to your .Xdefaults and then
always run hack in a window called hack

	xterm -name hack -e nethack

hack*vt100*geometry: 80x24
hack*vt100*scrollBar: off
hack*vt100.Translations: #override \
	<Key>F1: string("#c")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F2: string("#d")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F3: string("#f")string(0x0d)\n\
	Shift<Key>F3: string("#f")string(0x0d)string("y")\n\
	<Key>F4: string("#j")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F5: string("#l")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F6: string("#m")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F7: string("#o")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F8: string("#p")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>F9: string("#r")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>KP_F1: string("#t")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>KP_F2: string("#u")string(0x0d)\n\
	<Key>KP_F3: string("#w")string(0x0d)

This sets up the function keys to send extended commands. On a sun
